Spec: SpecDD Inline Completion Model

Platform: IntelliJ Platform / Kotlin

Purpose:
  Decide inline file path and local symbol completion for SpecDD body text.

Owns:
  ./SpecDDInlineCompletion.kt

Can modify:
  ./SpecDDInlineCompletion.kt

Can read:
  /src/test/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/completion/SpecDDInlineCompletionBehaviorSpec.kt

Must:
  Return no completion when the caret offset is outside the text.
  Detect the token prefix immediately before the caret using path and symbol characters.
  Return no completion for empty inline prefixes.
  Return matching VFS-backed file and directory path variants only for explicit path prefixes.
  Return project-root-relative variants for `/` prefixes.
  Return matching spec-file-relative variants for `./` and `../` prefixes.
  Cap path completion variants and skip common heavy directories while walking the project tree.
  Walk the project tree through IntelliJ VirtualFile entries, not local filesystem reads.
  Return matching local symbol variants from symbol-like tokens already present in the current SpecDD file.
  Keep file path variants before local symbol variants.
  Deduplicate variants while preserving first-seen order.
  Keep the model independent from IntelliJ editor registration.

Must not:
  Require cross-language IDE indexes.
  Report validation diagnostics.
  Define syntax highlighting colors.
